          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with onset at 61 years of age. The seizure type is focal to bilateral tonic-clonic, currently occurring approximately five times per week. The epilepsy is drug-responsive.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medication:\n- Zonisamide\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately five focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures per week.\n\nAssessment:\nFocal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. The etiology is genetic, associated with an SCN1A causative variant, c.5734C>T. The epilepsy is drug-responsive.\n\nPlan:\nContinue zonisamide as the current antiseizure medication. Continue monitoring seizure frequency and follow up in the epilepsy clinic.",
